<% content_for :title, "File" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Forms</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">File</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A file control: a drop area while nothing is chosen, and a file row once something is. The native
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;input type="file"&gt;</code> is the control and the
    only one — laid over the whole box, transparent, so a press anywhere opens the platform picker and a file dropped
    anywhere lands in it. Picking, dropping, <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">accept:</code>,
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">required:</code>, submission and the
    <%= link_to "Field", field_path, class: "text-primary underline" %> label are the platform's, and work with JavaScript
    off. <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">ui--file</code> adds what only script can: the
    swap to the file row, the drop target while dragging, and refusing a dropped file
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">accept:</code> doesn't allow — a browser applies it to
    its picker, never to a drop.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="file-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background grid items-start gap-8 p-12 mb-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
  <form id="file-form" class="grid gap-6">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "form[pdf]", required: true) do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "PDF" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::FileComponent, accept: "application/pdf,.pdf",
                            meta: "Fillable, flat or an ACORD copy · up to 20 MB and 40 pages",
                            drop_label: "Drop a PDF here or", choose_label: "Choose PDF") %>
    <% end %>
  </form>

  <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "edit[pdf]") do |field| %>
    <% field.with_label { "Replace the PDF" } %>
    <% field.with_control(Ui::FileComponent, accept: "application/pdf,.pdf",
                          filename: "ACORD_125_2016-03_partner_copy.pdf", file_meta: "372 KB · 4 pages",
                          choose_label: "Choose PDF") %>
    <% field.with_description { "Mapped fields the new PDF still has are kept." } %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# States %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Invalid and disabled</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  A Field's error marks the input <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-invalid</code>, and
  the box reads it; <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">disabled:</code> disables the input, so
  nothing opens, nothing drops and nothing submits.
</p>
<div id="file-states-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background grid items-start gap-8 p-12 mb-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
  <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "invalid[pdf]", errors: ["Choose a PDF to upload"]) do |field| %>
    <% field.with_label { "PDF" } %>
    <% field.with_control(Ui::FileComponent, accept: ".pdf", meta: "PDF only", choose_label: "Choose PDF") %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "disabled[pdf]") do |field| %>
    <% field.with_label { "PDF" } %>
    <% field.with_control(Ui::FileComponent, disabled: true, meta: "Uploads are paused") %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["name",         "String",  "required", "The input's HTML name. The id is derived from it the way form_with derives one; inside a Field both come from the Field."],
        ["accept",       "String",  "nil",      "The HTML accept list — \"application/pdf,.pdf\", \"image/*\". The picker filters by it, and ui--file refuses a dropped file it doesn't allow."],
        ["required",     "Boolean", "false",    "Native required on the input. Inside a Field, the Field's required: decides it."],
        ["disabled",     "Boolean", "false",    "Disables the input: nothing opens, drops or submits."],
        ["meta",         "String",  "nil",      "The drop area's one line under the sentence: what it takes, how big."],
        ["filename",     "String",  "nil",      "Renders the control already holding a file — the record's, on an edit form — as the file row. Choosing another replaces it; a reset puts it back."],
        ["file_meta",    "String",  "nil",      "The file row's line under that name: \"372 KB · 4 pages\". A file just picked shows its size; a host that knows more writes the row's meta on ui--file:chosen."],
        ["drop_label",   "String",  "nil",      "The drop area's sentence. Falls through to rails_ui_kit.file.drop_label."],
        ["choose_label", "String",  "nil",      "The drop area's button. Falls through to rails_ui_kit.file.choose_label."],
        ["change_label", "String",  "nil",      "The file row's button. Falls through to rails_ui_kit.file.change_label."],
        ["class",        "String",  "nil",      "Merged over the box's default classes — the caller always wins."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Accessibility %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="list-disc ps-5 space-y-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  <li>The native input is the one tab stop, named by the Field's label and described by its help and error. Enter or Space opens the picker, as on any file input, and a screen reader hears the file it holds from the input itself.</li>
  <li>Focus, invalid and disabled draw on the visible box from the input inside it, as an outline — never a box-shadow, which forced colours drop.</li>
  <li>The "Choose" and "Change" buttons are what a sighted user reads as the affordance; they are aria-hidden and out of the tab order, under the input that takes every press.</li>
</ul>
